## Required contract

{% work_unit title="Contact form example" %}
```json
{
  "id": "contact-form",
  "goal": "Create a production-ready contact form",
  "acceptanceCriteria": [
    "validates input",
    "tests pass"
  ],
  "constraints": [
    "follow existing Astro architecture"
  ],
  "risk": "medium",
  "preferredProvider": "auto",
  "dependencies": []
}
```
{% /work_unit %}

The full schema also preserves the raw request, business outcome, workflow, non-goals, assumptions, questions, classification, approvals, relevant documents and ADRs, first role, provider reason, documentation expectation, and routing status.

## Provider-neutral publication continuation

The compact `ContinuationPackage` carries a diff reference rather than a transcript plus the candidate branch/SHA, PR number when known, next authorized action, three readiness flags, required/completed/failed/outstanding gates, and bounded evidence references. Claude and Codex can stop, cap, or hand off without treating provider conversation history as system memory.

Completed checks remain reusable while the candidate SHA is unchanged. A SHA change deterministically removes candidate-bound completions and evidence, marks the affected readiness tier false, and returns those gates to the outstanding set. Stable external-control observations can remain referenced with a null candidate binding.
